From a442c83563561694c982cee60e9083de3d538d86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:39:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: 890M section says exactly what failed before the fix;
 protected-win effects quoted to the full first sentence

The README and the X1 release notes no longer say that no 27B model loads on the 890M without the fix. They name what was observed: GSQ IQ3_S and Q4_K_XL fail to load, IQ3_XXS loads for llama-bench but its server dies at init, and S-X8 was never run unfixed (inferred from the mechanism). The MUL_MAT_ID line says the matching 780M counts come from a lane-local receipt. The protected-wins table quoted effects cut at the first semicolon, which dropped qualifiers such as "serve-level TIED"; it now quotes each first sentence whole, and the CPU-path rows (-ngl 0) are labelled as such.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release documents for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched.
---
